@copilot Fix one remaining behavior regression on this PR directly. Work on its verified same-repository head branch `copilot/renovate-java-runtime-images`. Keep that branch; if GitHub assigns a follow-up branch, keep the platform-assigned branch. Do not start further tasks or request an additional PR.

The five Jib consumers now error on a missing `targetJDK` entry, and `smoke-tests/images/java-runtime-images.properties` stops at 27. Meanwhile `.github/workflows/reusable-pr-smoke-test-images.yml` and `.github/workflows/reusable-publish-smoke-test-images.yml` pass `LATEST_JAVA_VERSION` to those consumers; Renovate independently advances both `27 # renovate(java-version)` markers. The next normal feature bump can therefore select a major with no entry and break both image build and publish. Copilot review on head f8a00aafdb1a1c5fa9972a5eda66bc1866a8cdc3 had no findings; the issue above comes from tracing the reviewed diff to its existing callers.

Keep the automatically advancing latest-JDK case working without a human editing a separate mapping on every release. Ensure any image CI selects still has an explicit Renovate-managed reference and resolves to the same JDK major as the workflows and image tags. Consider deriving the relevant selectors and image reference from the same Renovate-managed source, or updating all associated fields atomically via Renovate. Keep existing fixed-major entries and their digest-pin automation, the currently selected tags/digests and test runtime majors, and existing intentional historical fixtures. Do not hand-bump any image, opt fixed matrix entries into major upgrades, or depend on the independent Temurin comparator PR. Validate that the simulated next feature-version update selects an extractable matching image and that the current selectors/builds and shared-file rebuild triggers still work. Keep the fix narrow.

@copilot Fix the remaining extraction and update issues on this PR directly on its existing same-repository head branch `copilot/renovate-java-runtime-images`. Keep that branch; if GitHub assigns a follow-up branch, keep the platform-assigned branch. Do not start further tasks or request any additional PRs.

The review confirmed that both properties-file managers use unsupported RE2 syntax: negative lookbehind in the fixed entries and named backreferences in the latest entry. Remove both, with no overlapping or false matches. A single explicit latest-role property with consumers deriving the Java major from its image tag is one way to avoid repeated fields; choose the smallest maintainable solution. Use the actual Renovate extractor/config validator with RE2, not Python/JavaScript-native regex or an extraction-only simulation. Confirm the current six shared images are extracted once each and an initial digest pin and a later digest update produce a reference the workflows and all relevant Gradle consumers can still read.

There is a second concrete blocker on the same path: the `eclipse-temurin-latest` alias still has `packageName: eclipse-temurin`, so Renovate's inherited Java LTS `allowedVersions` rule rejects the next feature major even though the PR sets `enabled: true` for major updates. Override the filter only for the explicit moving latest dependency and keep full rolling-tag version semantics; leave the fixed 8/11/17/21/25 entries, other deps, digest pinning, and branch-specific compatibility unchanged. Exercise actual Renovate update lookup/replacement with an available next non-LTS major in a controlled fixture and verify the resulting workflows use and publish the matching Jib runtime. The latest row must stay extractable after that next update. Do not change any current image tag or digest, move fixed test majors, depend on the separate Temurin comparator PR, or change unrelated CI Java policies. Report which Renovate engine checks ran and any environmental limits.

