@copilot Fix the digest-pinned latest-runtime selection on this PR directly on its existing same-repository head branch `copilot/renovate-java-runtime-images`. Keep the branch assigned by GitHub Copilot cloud agent; do not rename it or create a replacement branch. Keep any platform-assigned follow-up branch if GitHub creates one. Do not request an additional PR or dispatch other tasks.

The simplification is delivered in `3d098539`, but all five Jib builds call `substringAfterLast(':')` before `substringBefore('@')` when selecting the moving latest image. For `eclipse-temurin:27@sha256:aaaa...`, the last colon is the digest separator, so the code reads the hash instead of Java 27 and throws `Unsupported targetJDK: 27`. This is also the defect in Copilot review 5981884123 and the duplicate earlier finding 5981431015. Fix it in `smoke-tests/images/{grpc,play,quarkus,security-manager,spring-boot}/build.gradle.kts` by stripping the digest before extracting the tag. Keep the fix surgical, preserve the property-provider simplification, fixed-major precedence, unsupported-major failure, current image references and all other behavior. Do not add a general abstraction for this small correction.

Verify actual Gradle configuration for all five consumers with tag-only and digest-pinned latest images at Java 27 and a simulated next feature major. Include digest hashes beginning with a letter and a digit so accidentally parsing a hash cannot pass. Use project-property overrides and narrow configuration assertions on the selected full Jib base-image reference, not merely a separate reimplementation of the parser or attempts to pull a nonexistent future image. Verify an unmatched targetJDK is still rejected and ordinary fixed entries remain unchanged. Preserve both reusable workflows' agreement with the selected major. Report the executed checks and any environmental limits.
